   "date": "2023-11-17T23:38:27Z",
   "subject": "SEM for fertility",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>I have been having sleepless nights fitting this SEM model. One of the objectives to be achieved is to determine if social economic status (SES) has a direct impact on the fertility level of reproductive-aged women. </div><div>The following are the variables of interest: Total children ever born (TCEB), fertility preference (fertility), Wealth index, educational level, place of residence, ideal number of children, contraceptive use, religion, age at first birth, age at first cohabitation, number of living children (living), region, age at first sex (sex), and marital status. (See attached file).</div><div><br></div><div>Below was how I developed the model but was producing error. Kindly assist on how to sort this syntax.</div><div><br></div>myModel &lt;- &#39; # regressions<br>      TCEB+Fertility ~ SES+Demographic_Factors+Geo_Cultural_Factors+Ideal+Contraceptive<br>      SES ~ Reproductive_Behavior+Demographic_Factors<br>      Reproductive_Behavior ~ Demographic_Factors+Ideal<br><br>             # latent variable definitions <br># Measurement Model for SES (Latent Variable 1)<br>    SES =~ Wealth+Education+Residence<br><br>  # Measurement Model for Reproductive Behavior (Latent Variable 2)<br>    Reproductive_Behavior =~ TCEB+Fertility+Ideal+Contraceptive<br>  <br>  # Measurement Model for Demographic Factors (Latent Variable 3)<br>    Demographic_Factors =~ Cohabitation+Birth+Age<br>    <br>  # Measurement Model for Geographic and Cultural Factors (Latent Variable 5)<br>    Geo_Cultural_Factors =~ Region+Religion+Marital<br><br>             # variances and covariances <br>    SES ~~ Reproductive_Behavior<br>    SES ~~ Demographic_Factors<br>    Reproductive_Behavior ~~ Demographic_Factors<br>    TCEB ~~ Fertility<br>    Reproductive_Behavior ~~ Geo_Cultural_Factors<br>    Demographic_Factors ~~ Geo_Cultural_Factors<br><br>             # intercepts <br>               TCEB ~ 1 <br>               SES ~ 1<br>           &#39;<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
